==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Hightail Lizard}}
Hightail Lizards are common [[Lizard]]s that can be encountered in warm and temperate areas throughout [[Hyrule]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> They can be found basking on [[Tree]]s or [[Rock]]s, and they can also be startled out of hiding when [[Grass]] is cut. They often take a moment to register [[Link]]'s presence, but they flee quickly once they do.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> To catch them, Link can chase after them, use [[Stealth]] to approach them without being noticed, or stun them with an [[Arrow]] or [[Remote Bomb]].

Hightail Lizards can be [[Cooking|Cooked]] with [[Monster Part]]s in a [[Cooking Pot]] to make a [[Hasty Elixir]], which will temporarily grant Link [[Speed Up]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="BotW Inventory 2"/> Cooking them with other ingredients, however, will make [[Dubious Food]]. The [[Kochi Dye Shop]] will also accept them as ingredients for [[Brown Dye]].

Hightail Lizards are required to [[Enhancing|Enhance]] the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Hightail Lizard}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract/TotK|Hightail Lizard}}
Hightail Lizards can be found throughout the [[Surface]] of [[Hyrule]].

Hightail Lizards are required to [[Enhancing|Enhance]] the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|TotK|Hightail Lizard}}

